# minimum qore version
%requires qore >= 2.0
%requires yaml
%requires Util >= 3.0
%requires Logger
%requires HttpClientIo
%requires(reexport) ConnectionProvider >= 1.4

%modern

module YamlRpcClientIo {
    version = "1.0";
    desc = "Pure-Qore YAML-RPC client module with async I/O via HttpClientIo";
    author = "David Nichols <david@qore.org>";
    url = "http://qore.org";
    license = "MIT";
    init = sub () {
        ConnectionSchemeCache::registerScheme("yamlrpcio", YamlRpcIoConnection::ConnectionScheme);
        ConnectionSchemeCache::registerScheme("yamlrpcios", YamlRpcIoConnection::ConnectionScheme);
    };
}

/** @mainpage YamlRpcClientIo Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section yamlrpcclientiointro Introduction to the YamlRpcClientIo Module

    The %YamlRpcClientIo module provides a pure-Qore YAML-RPC client implementation using async I/O
    via \c HttpClientIo::HttpClientConnectionManager with automatic protocol negotiation
    (HTTP/3 &rarr; HTTP/2 &rarr; HTTP/1.1) and connection pooling.

    This module is the async I/O replacement for the
    \c YamlRpcClient class, providing the same YAML-RPC call API
    but with modern async networking.

    To use this module, use \c "%requires YamlRpcClientIo" in your code.

    All the public symbols in the module are defined in the YamlRpcClientIo namespace.

    The module provides the following classes:
    - @ref YamlRpcClientIo::YamlRpcClientIo "YamlRpcClientIo" - the main YAML-RPC client class
    - @ref YamlRpcClientIo::YamlRpcIoConnection "YamlRpcIoConnection" - connection provider for the
      ConnectionProvider framework

    @subsection yamlrpcclientio_features Features

    - Full YAML-RPC protocol support
    - Async I/O via \c HttpClientIo::HttpClientConnectionManager with automatic
      protocol negotiation (HTTP/3 &rarr; HTTP/2 &rarr; HTTP/1.1) and connection pooling
    - API-compatible with the \c YamlRpcClient class
    - Debug info variants for all call methods
    - ConnectionProvider integration with \c yamlrpcio:// and \c yamlrpcios:// URL schemes

    @subsection yamlrpcclientio_urls Endpoint URLs

    Both constructor forms select a fixed endpoint with @ref Util::get_http_endpoint_url(). An existing
    URL path, including an explicit <tt>/</tt>, wins over \c default_path. When the URL has no path,
    \c default_path supplies it (default: <tt>YAML</tt>); <tt>custom</tt> and <tt>/custom</tt> both
    select <tt>/custom</tt>, and an empty default selects <tt>/</tt>. A query or fragment alone is not
    a path: <tt>http://rpc.example.com?tenant=west#help</tt> selects <tt>/YAML?tenant=west</tt>.

    The query is preserved, including an empty <tt>?</tt>, duplicate parameters, and percent escapes.
    Fragments are removed. Existing internal/trailing slashes and dot segments are preserved; unsafe
    characters are percent-encoded once. The fallback is always a path on the same authority, never a
    URI reference or URL; query, fragment, NUL, and URI scheme syntax in it are rejected even when the
    URL already has a path. These rules apply after mapping the documented RPC scheme aliases to HTTP(S).

    \c getUrl() returns the selected endpoint URL, including the query and without the fragment. It can
    contain credentials: use \c Qore::get_safe_url() for display. These rules describe the Io clients;
    the native synchronous RPC clients retain their existing URL behavior.

    @subsection yamlrpcclientio_usage Usage Example

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires YamlRpcClientIo

YamlRpcClientIo client("http://localhost:8080/YAML");
auto result = client.call("system.listMethods");
printf("methods: %N\n", result);
client.close();
    @endcode

    @section yamlrpcclientio_relnotes Release History

    @subsection yamlrpcclientio_v1_0 YamlRpcClientIo v1.0
    - initial release
*/

#! the YamlRpcClientIo namespace holds all public definitions in the YamlRpcClientIo module
public namespace YamlRpcClientIo {
    #! Default URL path
    public const DefaultYamlRpcPath = "YAML";
}
